day_4:
 commencement and completion of Production Action Plan execution (Phase 1 & Phase 2):
 1. Diagnosed the root cause of the previous 2.21% mAP failure (train-vs-inference 4K-to-640 downscaling resolution collapse).
 2. Implemented tools/slice_dataset.py to pre-slice full drone frames into native 640x640 1:1 scale patches with 20% overlap, strict data-leakage split protection, box truncation filtering, and 15% hard negative mining (generated Dataset_tiled).
 3. Implemented tools/augment_rare_classes.py for Phase 2 synthetic class balancing, boosting minority classes (Rail Misalignment, Rail Wear, Rail Joint Damage, Damaged Fastener, Ballast Defect) to >= 150 instances each (1,280 total training patches).
 4. Redesigned train.py with production RT-DETR-L recipe (AdamW, cosine LR, close-mosaic=10, box=7.5, cls=0.5, dfl=1.5, max_det=300).
 5. Completed 35 epochs of production fine-tuning on NVIDIA RTX A4000 GPU (saved to models/rtdetr_production_tiled_best.pt).
 6. mAP@50 leaped from 2.21% to 36.25% on the held-out test split (a 16.4x improvement); Rail Crack mAP50 reached 59.2%, Rail Wear reached 79.7%, and Rail Misalignment reached 61.7%.
 7. Calibrated configs/pipeline_config.yaml (perform_standard_pred=False, conf=0.35, persistence=3) and verified 4K end-to-end benchmark latency at 502.97 ms (1.99 FPS, 15.71 ms/patch).

day_5:
 commencement and completion of Scale-Up Dataset Ingestion, Audit & Architecture Alignment:
 1. Received and audited initial Part 1 batch (577 images, 1,236 boxes); identified class deficiencies (1 Rail Wear, 0 Rail Misalignment).
 2. Ingested updated expanded dataset 'Dats set final version part 1.1' (899 images, 1,877 defect boxes, 202 clean negative images, 512x512 uniform resolution).
 3. Executed automated verification via scripts/audit_new_dataset.py; confirmed positive representation across all 9 canonical defect classes:
    - Sleeper Defect: 577 boxes
    - Damaged Fastener: 359 boxes (doubled from 179)
    - Foreign Objects: 301 boxes
    - Missing Fastener: 191 boxes (surged from 31)
    - Rail Crack: 154 boxes (tripled from 50)
    - Ballast Defect: 127 boxes
    - Rail Wear: 116 boxes (116x leap from 1)
    - Rail Joint Damage: 35 boxes
    - Rail Misalignment: 17 boxes (previously 0)
    - Clean Hard Negatives: 202 background patches (22.5% FP suppression bank)
 4. Mapped raw 11-class Roboflow taxonomy into canonical 9-class system (configs/dataset.yaml).
 5. Completed Dataset Consolidation via tools/remap_and_merge_part1_1.py:
    - Standardized Part 1.1's raw 11 Roboflow classes into canonical 9 classes per configs/dataset.yaml.
    - Merged with Dataset_tiled into Dataset_consolidated with strict train/valid/test split protection (zero cross-leakage confirmed via cryptographic MD5 hashing).
    - Total Consolidated Images: 2,544 (1,910 train, 432 valid, 202 test).
    - Total Defect Bounding Boxes: 4,293 (3,258 train, 689 valid, 346 test).
    - Hard Negatives: 352 background images (13.8% total, 238 in train) for false-positive suppression.
    - Representation milestone: Every single one of the 9 defect classes now has >= 168 boxes in train (Rail Misalignment: 168, Rail Joint Damage: 185, Ballast Defect: 266, Rail Wear: 240, Rail Crack: 339, Missing Fastener: 425, Damaged Fastener: 432, Foreign Objects: 451, Sleeper Defect: 752).
 6. Executed RT-DETR-L Production Fine-Tuning on NVIDIA RTX A4000 GPU across Dataset_consolidated (1,910 train, 432 val, 202 test):
    - Completed 50 epochs with AdamW, Cosine LR decay, and 10-epoch close-mosaic.
    - Test mAP@50 reached 53.75% (up from 36.25% on Day 4, a 17.5 percentage point increase).
    - Precision: 61.64%, Recall: 54.12%, mAP50-95: 31.22%.
    - Per-class performance: Rail Misalignment 74.2%, Ballast Defect 68.2%, Rail Wear 68.0%, Foreign Objects 65.2%, Rail Crack 51.4%, Damaged Fastener 48.1%, Missing Fastener 47.9%, Sleeper Defect 42.6%, Rail Joint Damage 18.1%.
    - Saved best checkpoint to models/rtdetr_consolidated_run_best.pt (66.25 MB).
 7. Compiled and Exported High-Throughput ONNX FP16 Engine:
    - Successfully compiled via tools/export_engine.py with onnxslim opset 18: models/rtdetr_consolidated_run_best.onnx (62.9 MB).
    - Calibrated configs/pipeline_config.yaml to activate new production weights.
 8. Established SavePoint & Tested 800px Frozen Experiment:
    - Created physical SavePoint snapshot at models/savepoints/day5_53map_baseline/.
    - Implemented tools/rollback_to_savepoint.py and automated promotion gate in train.py.
    - Tested 800px with 10 frozen backbone layers: Fasteners improved to 57.4% (P=72.5%) and Foreign Objects to 73.2%, but freezing low-level layers degraded long-range track geometry (Misalignment 20.0%, Crack 22.4%), resulting in 44.08% overall mAP.
    - SavePoint Promotion Gate automatically triggered, blocking deployment and keeping 53.75% model safe.
 9. SavePoint Restoration & Cleanup:
    - Executed tools/rollback_to_savepoint.py; confirmed Day 5 production model models/rtdetr_consolidated_run_best.pt (53.75% mAP50) is actively restored in configs/pipeline_config.yaml.
    - Purged experimental artifacts (deleted models/rtdetr_consolidated_800_frozen_best.pt, runs/detect/runs/rtdetr_consolidated_800_frozen, and runs/detect/val-3).
    - Dropped all secondary YOLO/hybrid plans per user specification; remaining 100% committed to RT-DETR-L.
    - Completed deep dataset audit (scripts/analyze_dataset_deep.py) and authored DATASET_V2_PREPARATION_AND_QUALITY_GUIDE.md detailing the +280 to +350 targeted image expansion roadmap to reach >= 85-90% accuracy.
 10. Current Active Baseline: models/rtdetr_consolidated_run_best.pt (53.75% mAP50) in configs/pipeline_config.yaml. Ready for app.py dashboard testing.

day_6:
 commencement and completion of Final Version Dataset (Railway_defect_dataset_1200) Ingestion, Cross-Merging & Retraining:
 1. Received user request to remove previous final dataset ('Dats set final version part 1.1') and adopt new 1200+ images dataset ('Railway_defect_dataset_1200') as final set version, training model with this and pre dataset.
 2. Verified removal of 'Dats set final version part 1.1' and purged legacy Dataset_consolidated.
 3. Audited 'Railway_defect_dataset_1200' (1,237 images, 3,184 defect boxes, 202 clean negative images, 15 Roboflow classes).
 4. Developed and executed tools/remap_and_merge_v3_1200.py:
    - Remapped 15 raw Roboflow classes to canonical 9 classes (configs/dataset.yaml).
    - Cross-referenced with Dataset_pre via MD5 hashing: resolved 252 overlapping images to latest v3 annotations without duplicate conflicts, and integrated 44 unique field images into the train split (+69 defect boxes).
    - Generated new Dataset_consolidated: 1,281 images (919 train, 236 valid, 126 test), 3,253 defect boxes, 217 clean background negatives (16.9%).
    - Cryptographically verified 0.00% data leakage across train, valid, and test splits (0 images).
 5. Launched RT-DETR-L production fine-tuning on NVIDIA RTX A4000 GPU (50 epochs, batch 8, imgsz 640, AdamW, cosine LR, 10 close-mosaic):
    - Checkpoint saved to models/rtdetr_v3_1200_consolidated_best.pt (66.25 MB).
    - Evaluated on held-out test split (126 images, 339 instances): mAP@50 reached 51.22%, mAP@50-95 reached 33.49% (surpassing Day 5's 31.22%), Precision 58.62%, Recall 50.97%.
    - Key defect leaps: Rail Joint Damage surged from 18.1% to 40.2% (>2x leap), Ballast Defect 85.3%, Foreign Objects 76.8%, Rail Misalignment 64.2%.
 6. Compiled and exported optimized high-throughput ONNX FP16 engine via export_engine.py with onnxslim opset 18: models/rtdetr_v3_1200_consolidated_best.onnx (62.9 MB).
 7. SavePoint Protection Gate: Day 5 baseline (53.75% mAP50) remains safely active in configs/pipeline_config.yaml, while Day 6 model (models/rtdetr_v3_1200_consolidated_best.pt / .onnx) is fully preserved for comparative analysis and inference.

day_7:
 commencement and completion of Dedicated Standalone Web Application (RailSamiksha_Production_App) Extraction & Deployment Build:
 1. Extracted 53.75% mAP50 master model weights (models/rtdetr_consolidated_run_best.pt, 66.25 MB) and slimmed ONNX FP16 engine (models/rtdetr_consolidated_run_best.onnx, 62.9 MB) into RailSamiksha_Production_App/weights/.
 2. Built self-contained production architecture with SAHI 1:1 scale patch slicer (core/slicer.py), Non-Maximum Merging (core/merger.py), ByteTrack 3-hit temporal flicker filter (core/tracker.py), RTK-GPS telemetry parser (core/telemetry.py), and unified pipeline (core/pipeline.py).
 3. Authored modern aerospace-grade dark UI Streamlit application (app.py) supporting:
    - Tab 1: High-Resolution Aerial Still Frame Inspection with 4K SAHI tiling, defect crop inspection gallery, and metrics HUD.
    - Tab 2: Aerial Patrol Video Inspection with real-time ByteTrack temporal deduplication, telemetry HUD, and live incident table.
    - Tab 3: Georeferenced Defect Map with interactive RTK-GPS track corridor plotting.
    - Tab 4: P-Way Maintenance Incident Registry with severity cards and 1-click CSV report export.
 4. Packaged pre-loaded sample drone patrol assets in samples/ (sample_track_flight.mp4, sample_track_image.jpg, Ballast Washout, Broken Track, Defective clips).
 5. Configured portable execution and deployment assets: 1-click Windows launcher (run_app.bat, run_app.py), cloud container spec (Dockerfile), and dependencies (requirements.txt).
 6. Completed end-to-end dry-run verification on GPU (cuda:0) for both still and video inference.
 7. Commencement and completion of RT-DETR-L 50-epoch retraining with verified notebook recipe (train_canonical_85.py):
    - Installed albumentations (v2.0.8) activating out-of-the-box transforms: Blur, MedianBlur, ToGray, and CLAHE.
    - Set explicit absolute paths in Dataset_consolidated/data.yaml (1,281 images, 9 canonical classes).
    - Executed 50 epochs on NVIDIA RTX A4000 GPU (0.563 hrs) with batch=16, AdamW (lr0=0.000769, momentum=0.9), amp=True, freeze=None.
    - Achieved 50.74% mAP@50 and 32.48% mAP@50-95 on held-out test split (126 images, 339 instances):
      * Rail Misalignment: 75.0% mAP50
      * Foreign Objects: 72.8% mAP50
      * Ballast Defect: 71.2% mAP50
      * Damaged Fastener: 54.1% mAP50
      * Rail Wear: 46.7% mAP50
      * Rail Joint Damage: 40.1% mAP50
      * Rail Crack: 39.5% mAP50
      * Sleeper Defect: 32.2% mAP50
      * Missing Fastener: 24.9% mAP50
    - Checkpoint saved to models/rtdetr_v3_canonical_85_best.pt (66.3 MB) and runs/detect/runs/detect/runs/rtdetr_v3_canonical_85/weights/best.pt.
    - Exported optimized high-throughput ONNX FP16 engine with onnxslim: models/rtdetr_v3_canonical_85_best.onnx (62.9 MB, 16.6 ms inference latency).
